| LAB #7 - Problem 3: In-Place Array Sorting
| Team Cooked, Not Cooking
| - Badiola, Enrique Gabriel
| - Paras, Riva Kaitleen
| - Sy, Wencarll Cynric 
|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||

.include beta.uasm

| Bubble sort, smallest first. Compare two neighbors; if they are in the wrong
| order, swap them. After each pass, the biggest number of the unsorted part has
| moved to the end, so the next pass can stop one place earlier.
|
| r0 = N (how many numbers there are)
| r1 = where the unsorted part ends 
| r2 = where we are now
| r3 = the left number, r4 = the right number, r5 = yes/no answer of a compare
| Number k (k = 1..N) is found at ARRAY + 4*k, and ARRAY + 0 holds N.

        LD(ARRAY, r0)           | r0 = N
        SHLC(r0, 2, r1)         | r1 = 4*N = offset of the last number

OUTER:  CMPLEC(r1, 4, r5)       | is there 1 or 0 numbers left to sort?
        BNE(r5, DONE)           | yes -> the array is sorted, stop
        CMOVE(4, r2)            | start at the first number

INNER:  CMPLT(r2, r1, r5)       | is there a number to the right of us?
        BEQ(r5, NEXT)           | no -> this pass is finished
        LD(r2, ARRAY, r3)       | r3 = number on the left
        LD(r2, ARRAY+4, r4)     | r4 = number on the right
        CMPLT(r4, r3, r5)       | is the right one smaller than the left one?
        BEQ(r5, SKIP)           | no -> already in order, don't swap
        ST(r4, ARRAY, r2)       | put the smaller one on the left
        ST(r3, ARRAY+4, r2)     | put the bigger one on the right
SKIP:   ADDC(r2, 4, r2)         | move one number to the right
        BR(INNER)

NEXT:   SUBC(r1, 4, r1)         | the last number is now in place, so look at one less
        BR(OUTER)

DONE:   HALT()

|||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||||

. = 0x19C

ARRAY:
        LONG(7)                 | <-- length of the array
        LONG(5)
        LONG(7)
        LONG(8)
        LONG(6)
        LONG(4)
        LONG(9)
        LONG(3)
